  note = {First DOM-downsampling algorithm as a DOM-snapshot preprocessing step for token-cost reduction. Downsampled DOM (67\% SR) matches a grounded GUI-screenshot baseline (65\%) at the same token order ($10^3$), and exceeds it by 8\% one order higher ($10^4$); concludes the DOM-inherent hierarchy is a strong UI feature for LLMs. Cited in our paper \S 1/\S 6 cost argument as independent external corroboration that a DOM/text representation matches or beats a pixel-screenshot baseline at equal token budget --- the same cost-vs-representation logic behind our phantom-SoM cost $\approx$ DOM claim. The digest under-rated this (Score 1); it is the closest of the related GUI-grounding papers to our cost positioning.}
