  note = {Browser-native React ``Android-like'' simulator (28 apps / 416 task templates / $>$27k instances); judge = per-task Python check over a structured state diff (deterministic, sub-ms); AnswerSheet protocol replaces free-text answer matching with typed form matchers, targeting false-reject (paraphrase) and false-accept (CoT gold-answer leakage substring) failures. VLM-judge error measured at 10.2\% (12/118; two judge models agree on the count, partially different subsets). Qwen3-VL-4B-Instruct (our B1 backbone) scores 9.4$\pm$0.6\% SR --- a cross-domain low-capability anchor. Cited in thesis lit-review (judge-reliability line). Preprint; id verified via API 2026-06-10.}
